    "id": "blog-2",
    "title": "How JSON File Storage Works",
    "slug": "how-json-file-storage-works",
    "excerpt": "For early development, the API persists records to local JSON files instead of a database.",
    "content": "Each collection (blogs, pages, settings, about) maps to a JSON file under backend/data. Create, update, and delete operations rewrite the file so changes survive server restarts.\n\nWhen you are ready for production, swap the JSON store for a real database with the same route shapes.",
